andler, and this assessment does not treat the crop as deployment/runtime proof that the upstream binding occurred in the assessed request.","facts":[{"id":"fact-entry","kind":"entry","statement":"The GET /items/{id} route enters read_item with session, current_user, and id parameters.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-3df5de8f43bc9c54","startLine":48,"endLine":49}]},{"id":"fact-principal-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The supplied source defines CurrentUser as a User dependency on get_current_user; that function resolves a user, rejects a missing or inactive user, and otherwise returns the user. This is source-visible dependency wiring, not proof of runtime or deployment binding for a particular request.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-ec26811e863df154","startLine":30,"endLine":49}]},{"id":"fact-resource-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"read_item retrieves the Item identified by id and raises 404 when no such item exists.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-3df5de8f43bc9c54","startLine":53,"endLine":55}]},{"id":"fact-authorization-control","kind":"control","statement":"The strongest visible item-read authorization control raises 403 only when the caller is not a superuser and the item's owner differs from the caller.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-3df5de8f43bc9c54","startLine":56,"endLine":57}]},{"id":"fact-superuser-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"Because the denial predicate begins with not current_user.is_superuser, a caller satisfying the task's superuser premise makes that conjunct false even when ownership differs.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-3df5de8f43bc9c54","startLine":56,"endLine":57}]},{"id":"fact-protected-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"When neither the not-found branch nor the authorization-denial branch terminates execution, read_item returns the retrieved item, permitting the read.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-3df5de8f43bc9c54","startLine":53,"endLine":58}]}],"decisiveMissingFacts":[],"suggestedObservations":[]}]}}],"tokens